Hi all,

after a long time, I've recently started a new character again; I'm 
giving a new try at an atheist priest (which should not be too hard, I 
hope -- I'm not usually a conduct player, except that I never wish for 
artifacts or genocide monsters).

So far, it looks quite good (just cleared the mines and Sokoban -- and 
guess what, I got a BoH plus three other ones lying in the mines...). 
Now I wonder about strategy for the mid-game (and possibly later the 
end-game).

The wiki states that it may be hard for priests to find a good weapon; 
and as an atheist, I also can't sacrifice to get artifacts (and don't 
want to wish for any).  I could possibly have dipped for Excalibur, but 
didn't think about it and now I'm already an elf.

Currently I'm using a trident, which seems to work out quite well 
(previously I used my starting mace).  Do you think that should do it 
through the game?  Or what would be a better choice -- I thought about a 
unicorn horn as alternative so far.  Anything else?

Later on, I can of course try to cast attack spells as well; but I fear 
that power will not be enough in order to do that "mainly" and without 
the Eye.

Another question:  I found some rather nice armour (the intrinsic BUC 
knowledge is really nice!) and am down at AC -9 now with dwarvish 
mithril, large shield, helmet and boots.  This is quite nice, but I 
wonder whether (or when) I should start switching metal items for 
cast-friendly ones.  At the moment I don't really know many spells (and 
also no very useful ones) -- but I feel that it may be too long to wait 
for some kind of DSM to replace the mithril.  Do you think I should 
switch to leather armor for the possibility of casting spells?  Or 
really stick to mithril until I can get my hands on DSM?

